{"schemaVersion":2,"sectionID":20018097,"chapterID":15000203,"chapterNumber":"II-3","sectionNumber":"23-443","title":"Special provisions in other geographies","officialText":"","previewText":"Special provisions for zoning lots adjoining public parks In all districts, where a building adjoining a public park utilizes the provisions of Section 23-381, such public park shall be considered a wide street for the purpose of applying the regulations set forth in Sections 23-42 and 23-43 to any building or other structure on a zoning lot adjoining such public park. Special provisions for zoning lots with transpor","blocks":[{"id":"zr-18097-block-001","kind":"html","html":"<ol><li>Special provisions for <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> adjoining <strong><em>public parks</em></strong><br><br>\n\tIn all districts, where a <strong><em>building</em></strong> adjoining a <strong><em>public park</em></strong> utilizes the provisions of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-381\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-381\"><span>23-381</span></a>, such <strong><em>public park</em></strong> shall be considered a <strong><em>wide street</em></strong> for the purpose of applying the regulations set forth in Sections <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-42\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-42\"><span>23-42</span></a> and <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-43\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-43\"><span>23-43</span></a> to any <strong><em>building or other structure</em></strong> on a <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> adjoining such <strong><em>public park</em></strong>.&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>Special provisions for <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> with <strong><em>transportation-infrastructure-adjacent frontage</em></strong><br><br>\n\tFor <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> or portions thereof within 100 feet of a <strong><em>street line</em></strong> along a <strong><em>transportation-infrastructure-adjacent frontage</em></strong>, the following shall apply:\n\t<ol><li>the applicable <strong><em>street wall</em></strong> location provisions of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-431\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-431\"><span>23-431</span></a> and the minimum base height provisions of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-432\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-432\"><span>23-432</span></a> need not apply; and</li>\n\t\t<li>for <strong><em>buildings</em></strong> containing <strong><em>multiple dwelling residences</em></strong> that are not otherwise eligible for additional height pursuant to Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-434\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-434\"><span>23-434</span></a>, the applicable maximum <strong><em>building</em></strong> heights may be increased by 10 feet in R1 through R6 Districts, and by 20 feet in R7 through R12 Districts.&nbsp;</li>\n\t</ol></li>\n\t<li><strong><em>Limited Height Districts</em></strong><br><br>\n\tIn the <strong><em>Limited Height Districts</em></strong>, the underlying height and setback regulations for the zoning district shall apply, except that:&nbsp;\n\t<ol><li>the additional height allowances for eligible sites set forth in Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-434\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3#23-434\"><span>23-434</span></a> shall not apply; and</li>\n\t\t<li>for <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> that do not contain <strong><em>qualifying affordable housing</em></strong> or <strong><em>qualifying senior housing</em></strong>, the maximum height of <strong><em>buildings or other structures</em></strong> shall be as shown in the following table:<br>\n\t\t&nbsp;\n\t\t<table class=\"Table\" style=\"margin-left:100px; border-collapse:collapse\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:162px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in; border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"color:black\"><strong><em>Limited height district</em></strong></span></b></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:336px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in; border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p align=\"right\" style=\"text-align:right\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Maximum height above <strong><em>curb level</em></strong> or <strong><em>base plane</em></strong>, as applicable</span></b></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:none; width:162px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in; border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">LH-1</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:none; width:336px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in; border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p align=\"right\" style=\"text-align:right\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">50 feet</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"width:162px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">LH-lA</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"width:336px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p align=\"right\" style=\"text-align:right\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">60 feet</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"width:162px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">LH-2</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"width:336px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p align=\"right\" style=\"text-align:right\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">70 feet</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"width:162px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">LH-3</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"width:336px; padding:0in 8px 0in 8px; height:.3in\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p align=\"right\" style=\"text-align:right\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">100 feet</span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t</tr></tbody></table></li>\n\t</ol></li>\n\t<li>Special provisions along certain district boundaries<br><br>\n\tWhere a <strong><em>lot line</em></strong> of a <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> located in an R6 through R12 District coincides with the district boundary of an R1 through R5 District, the height of a <strong><em>building</em></strong> within a ‘transition area’ measured parallel to the district boundary, shall not exceed the heights set forth in the table, depending on the zoning district adjacency, the adjacent <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> condition, and the width of the <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong>.&nbsp;<br>\n\t&nbsp;\n\t<p align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center; margin-left:48px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">TRANSITION AREA DIMENSION AND MAXIMUM HEIGHT</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n\t<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border:none\"><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:240px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:58px; border-top:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:384px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:58px; border-top:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Maximum permitted height within transition area </span></span></span></b></span></span></span><br><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">(in feet, above <strong><em>base plane</em></strong>)</span></span></span></b></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t</tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:240px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:92px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Adjacent zoning district and <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> condition</span></span></span></b></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:150px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:92px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> with a <strong><em>lot width</em></strong> less than or equal to 30 feet</span></span></span></b></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:234px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:92px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> with a <strong><em>lot width</em></strong> greater than 30 feet</span></span></span></b></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:150px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:55px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Within a distance equal to one-third of the <strong><em>lot width</em></strong> of the district boundary</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:108px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:55px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Within 15 feet of the district boundary</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:126px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:55px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Beyond 15 feet and within 25 feet of the district boundary</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t</tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:96px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">R1&nbsp; R2&nbsp; R3 </span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:144px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Non-<strong><em>qualifying residential sites</em></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:150px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">45*</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:108px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">45*</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:126px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">65</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:144px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong><em>Qualifying residential sites</em></strong> </span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:150px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">65</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:108px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">65</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:126px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">85</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t</tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:96px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">R4&nbsp; R5 </span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:144px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Non-<strong><em>qualifying residential sites</em></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:150px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">65</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:108px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">65</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:126px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">85</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:144px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong><em>Qualifying residential sites</em></strong> </span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:150px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">85</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:108px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">85</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:126px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:38px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">85</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t</tr></tbody></table><p style=\"margin-left:42px; text-indent:-31.5pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">*&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> in R7, R8, R9 and R10 Districts, the maximum permitted height within the transition area shall be 65 feet. </span></span></span></p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>","plainText":"Special provisions for zoning lots adjoining public parks In all districts, where a building adjoining a public park utilizes the provisions of Section 23-381, such public park shall be considered a wide street for the purpose of applying the regulations set forth in Sections 23-42 and 23-43 to any building or other structure on a zoning lot adjoining such public park. Special provisions for zoning lots with transportation-infrastructure-adjacent frontage For zoning lots or portions thereof within 100 feet of a street line along a transportation-infrastructure-adjacent frontage, the following shall apply: the applicable street wall location provisions of Section 23-431 and the minimum base height provisions of Section 23-432 need not apply; and for buildings containing multiple dwelling residences that are not otherwise eligible for additional height pursuant to Section 23-434, the applicable maximum building heights may be increased by 10 feet in R1 through R6 Districts, and by 20 feet in R7 through R12 Districts. Limited Height Districts In the Limited Height Districts, the underlying height and setback regulations for the zoning district shall apply, except that: the additional height allowances for eligible sites set forth in Section 23-434 shall not apply; and for zoning lots that do not contain qualifying affordable housing or qualifying senior housing, the maximum height of buildings or other structures shall be as shown in the following table: Limited height district Maximum height above curb level or base plane, as applicable LH-1 50 feet LH-lA 60 feet LH-2 70 feet LH-3 100 feet Special provisions along certain district boundaries Where a lot line of a zoning lot located in an R6 through R12 District coincides with the district boundary of an R1 through R5 District, the height of a building within a ‘transition area’ measured parallel to the district boundary, shall not exceed the heights set forth in the table, depending on the zoning district adjacency, the adjacent zoning lot condition, and the width of the zoning lot. TRANSITION AREA DIMENSION AND MAXIMUM HEIGHT Maximum permitted height within transition area (in feet, above base plane) Adjacent zoning district and zoning lot condition For zoning lots with a lot width less than or equal to 30 feet For zoning lots with a lot width greater than 30 feet Within a distance equal to one-third of the lot width of the district boundary Within 15 feet of the district boundary Beyond 15 feet and within 25 feet of the district boundary R1 R2 R3 Non-qualifying residential sites 45* 45* 65 Qualifying residential sites 65 65 85 R4 R5 Non-qualifying residential sites 65 65 85 Qualifying residential sites 85 85 85 * For zoning lots in R7, R8, R9 and R10 Districts, the maximum permitted height within the transition area shall be 65 feet."}],"zoning":{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceNodeID":18097,"sourcePath":"/article-ii/chapter-3/23-443","sourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-3/23-443","sourceContentHash":"29a8a1aa19efa0a190125169cfe42769df17323ed4c56594fa402fee3147fd92","article":{"roman":"II","title":"Residence District Regulations"},"chapter":{"number":"3","title":"Residential Bulk Regulations in Residence Districts","canonicalNumber":"II-3"},"appendix":null,"subsections":[],"tables":[{"id":"zr-18097-table-001","ordinal":0,"sourceAnchor":null,"caption":null,"plainText":"Limited height district Maximum height above curb level or base plane, as applicable LH-1 50 feet LH-lA 60 feet LH-2 70 feet LH-3 100 feet","contentHash":"0208e4f171488a1aca1365f4dbd48435c6256cb9f59ee5c229bf01d3c1de3453"},{"id":"zr-18097-table-002","ordinal":1,"sourceAnchor":null,"caption":null,"plainText":"Maximum permitted height within transition area (in feet, above base plane) Adjacent zoning district and zoning lot condition For zoning lots with a lot width less than or equal to 30 feet For zoning lots with a lot width greater than 30 feet Within a distance equal to one-third of the lot width of the district boundary Within 15 feet of the district boundary Beyond 15 feet and within 25 feet of the district boundary R1 R2 R3 Non-qualifying residential sites 45* 45* 65 Qualifying residential sites 65 65 85 R4 R5 Non-qualifying residential sites 65 65 85 Qualifying residential sites 85 85 85","contentHash":"57aab235b7b29471458c959073641e195911f5eba617577651439703fdf76c84"}],"mapReferences":[],"appendixReferences":[],"specialDistrict":null,"amendmentHistory":[{"effectiveDate":"2024-12-05","reportNumber":"N240290ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20240290%20ZRY","projectName":"City of Yes for Housing Opportunity","action":"Amended","notes":"Provisions for zoning lots adjoining public parks and within Limited Height Districts relocated from former Sections 23-671 and 23-691; new provisions proposed for zoning lots with transportation-infrastructure-adjacent frontage","description":"An amendment modifying multiple Sections to expand opportunities for housing within all zoning districts, and across all 59 of the City’s Community Districts"},{"effectiveDate":"1994-06-29","reportNumber":"N940257ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20940257%20ZRY","projectName":"QUALITY HOUSING FOLLOW-UP TEXT","action":"Amended","notes":"Quality Housing; moved from 23-69","description":"TEXT CHANGES TO MODIFY THE ZONING CONTROLS GOVERNING THE DEVELOPMENT OF QUALITY HOUSING BLDGS & THE DEVELOPMENT OF ALL BLDGS CITYWIDE & CREATE NEW C6-3X, R10X & C6-4X DISTS"},{"effectiveDate":"1989-06-29","reportNumber":"N890552ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20890552%20ZRY","projectName":"LOWER DENSITY CONTEXTUAL ZONING","action":"Deleted","notes":"Lower density","description":"TEXT CHANGE TO R3-1,R3-2,R4 & R5 DISTRICTS & CREATION OF SIX NEW LOWER DENSITY CONTEXTUAL ZONING DISTRICTS WHICH ARE MAPPED IN ALL BOROUGHS OTHER THAN MANHATTAN"},{"effectiveDate":"1973-11-15","reportNumber":"CP22452","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=CP%2022452","projectName":null,"action":"Amended","notes":null,"description":null},{"effectiveDate":"1973-03-08","reportNumber":"CP21965A","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=CP%2021965a","projectName":null,"action":"Added","notes":null,"description":null}],"amendmentHistorySourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/ajax/get/amendment/section/18097","effectiveDate":"2024-12-05","lastAmended":"2024-12-05","version":"NYC Zoning Resolution — text through 2026-08-13","researchEligibility":false}}
